# Restart API after backend changes

When you change code that the running API process will not pick up reliably, **restart the API yourself** in the same session. Do not tell the user to restart manually.

## Restart when

- Edits under `apps/api/`, `packages/ingest/`, `packages/shared/`, or `packages/db/` that affect runtime behavior
- `.env` changes (tsx watch does not reload env)
- The user reports stale API behavior after your changes

`tsx watch` usually reloads API **code** edits; still restart after ingest/shared/db changes or if health check fails.

## How to restart (API only)

Prefer restarting **only** `:4000` so web (`:3000`) keeps running:

```bash
lsof -nP -iTCP:4000 -sTCP:LISTEN -t 2>/dev/null | xargs kill -9 2>/dev/null
sleep 1
cd /Users/eric/Code/bored && pnpm dev:api
```

Run `pnpm dev:api` in the background. Verify:

```bash
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:4000/health
```

Use `pnpm dev:restart` only when both web and API need a fresh env (e.g. after `.env` edits).

## Do not

- Leave "restart the API" as a user TODO when you could do it
- Spawn duplicate API listeners (always free `:4000` first)
